# =============================================================================
# OPSEC: Third sweep — upstream/ restored with key files gitignored
# upstream/ is vendored reference code required by go.mod replace directives.
# The 3 private key files are gitignored (both by *.key above and the specific
# patterns below). The corresponding .crt files are whitelisted for tracking
# because they are public self-signed test certificates needed by TLS tests.
#
# Bug report (v3.4.3): RSA private keys were committed to public GitHub.
# Remediation: keys rotated, *.key pattern blocks re-commit, pre-commit hook
# scans for PRIVATE KEY string.
# =============================================================================

# Private keys in upstream/ (explicit patterns — redundant with *.key above,
# but documented here so future maintainors understand WHY upstream/ is
# safe to track while these files must never be re-added).
upstream/aegisgate/pkg/adapters/certs/server.key
upstream/aegisgate/pkg/adapters/custom-certs/server.key
upstream/aegisgate/pkg/proxy/certs/ca/ca.key

# Whitelist the corresponding public certificates (*.crt is globally
# gitignored, but these self-signed test certs need to be tracked so
# that the upstream TLS packages can find them at test time).
!upstream/aegisgate/pkg/adapters/certs/server.crt
!upstream/aegisgate/pkg/adapters/custom-certs/server.crt
!upstream/aegisgate/pkg/proxy/certs/ca/ca.crt

